--| Outbound HTTP, as a context a host provides.

  Code that makes requests declares `[Async, Http]` and calls the functions of [`http`](http), which come
  from whichever `Http` instance its caller supplies. The console host (`nanyx.cli.host`) supplies
  one to the program's entry point; a host that doesn't provide it guarantees that nothing in the
  program reaches the network. A library depends on `nanyx.http` and imports
  `nanyx.http/client`.
export module client

import (
  nanyx/async as (Async)
  nanyx.http/request as (Request)
  nanyx.http/response as (Response)
)

--| Why a request had no response: none came in the request's `timeout`, the server couldn't be
  reached (with what the system said), the URL isn't an absolute `http` or `https` one, the task it
  was made in was cancelled, as a task `race` lost is, or another reason, described.
export type HttpError =
  | #timeout
  | #connectionFailed(string)
  | #invalidUrl
  | #cancelled
  | #other(string)

--| Outbound HTTP, which a host supplies. Its member is what a host implements; code calls the
  functions of [`http`](http), which are written on it.
export context Http = (
  --| Sends `request`, waiting for its response. Only the instance that sends it waits.
  sendRequest: [Async] Request -> #some(Response) | HttpError
)
